  Check migrations for statements that lock tables, rewrite them or break running code.

  With no arguments, migrail finds the migrations in the repository and detects the migration tool.
  Pass migration files or directories to check only those, or - to read SQL from standard input.

  [1mUsage[m
    migrail check [path]... | - [flags]

  [1mFlags[m
        [1m--all[m                 check every migration, not only the ones changed since the
                              base branch
        [1m--base string[m         git branch or commit to compare against (default: origin/HEAD,
                              main or master)
        [1m--ci[m                  CI mode: no color, links or spinners unless forced
        [1m--compact[m             print one line per finding
        [1m--db-version string[m   PostgreSQL major version in production, such as 16 (default: 12)
    [1m-d, --dir string[m          project root to search for migrations (default: the repository
                              root)
        [1m--fail-on string[m      exit with code 1 on findings at or above: error, warning,
                              notice or never (default "error")
    [1m-f, --format string[m       output format: pretty, json, sarif or github (default "pretty")
        [1m--framework string[m    migration tool to use instead of detecting it: sqitch, atlas,
                              prisma, drizzle, goose, dbmate, golang-migrate, flyway, sql
    [1m-q, --quiet[m               print only findings and the summary
    [1m-r, --rule strings[m        only run these rules, by ID or slug
        [1m--skip-rule strings[m   skip these rules, by ID or slug
    [1m-v, --verbose[m             print each phase with its timing

  [1mGlobal flags[m
        [1m--ascii[m           use ASCII symbols instead of Unicode
        [1m--color string[m    use color: auto, always or never (default "auto")
        [1m--no-hyperlinks[m   don't print clickable file links
        [1m--theme string[m    color theme: auto, dark, light or mono (default "auto")
